                {
                    "project_id": 25684254,
                    "id": 140572251,
                    "iid": 9,
                    "title": "Relax the isinstance check of openphi.read_region() method",
                    "description": "Thanks for your work! Lately colleagues stumbled upon a convertibility difference between openslide and openphi when it comes to the read_region() method. OpenSlide appears to accept integral types such as numpy.int32 which fail the isinstance check at line openphi.py line 279 and 280. \nThis matters when using other work written with openslide in mind such as CLAM (https://github.com/mahmoodlab/CLAM).\nDo you think it makes sense to relax the isinstance check in order to align more with the openslide package?\nE. g. checking against numbers.Integral instead of checking againt int.\n\nSome testing shows compatibility with openslide when switching to checking against numbers.Integral for the datatypes:\nnp.int32, np.int64, np.uint32, np.uint64 (all work with openslide but not openphi)\nand float, np.float32, np.float64 (neither work with openslide or openphi)",
                    "state": "closed",
                    "created_at": "2024-01-09T14:26:02.728Z",
                    "updated_at": "2024-02-02T12:44:41.573Z",
