                {
                    "project_id": 25684254,
                    "id": 124339283,
                    "iid": 8,
                    "title": "Add an openslide's function get_best_level_for_downsample. More compatible with openslide.",
                    "description": "Hello. I am using openphi for my experiment. Adding this function can make it more compatible with openslide.\nThe code comes from here.\nhttps://github.com/bayer-science-for-a-better-life/tiffslide/blob/main/tiffslide/tiffslide.py#L248\n```python\n\ndef get_best_level_for_downsample(self, downsample: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"return the best level for a given downsampling factor\"\"\"\n    if downsample <= 1.0:\n        return 0\n    for lvl, ds in enumerate(self.level_downsamples):\n        if ds > downsample:\n            return lvl - 1\n    return self.level_count - 1\n```",
                    "state": "closed",
                    "created_at": "2023-02-27T08:49:55.412Z",
                    "updated_at": "2023-03-09T15:31:40.284Z",
