                {
                    "project_id": 25684254,
                    "id": 124237228,
                    "iid": 7,
                    "title": "Open mode file",
                    "description": "Hello :smile: \n\nI'm the developer of the rust library [philips-isyntax-rs](https://github.com/AzHicham/philips-isyntax-rs)\nI saw that you open a [IsyntaxFacade with \"ficom\" mode ](https://gitlab.com/BioimageInformaticsGroup/openphi/-/blob/master/openphi/openphi.py#L55) from my understanding, passing a empty string is equivalent to \"caching-ficom\" mode, see [here](https://github.com/AzHicham/philips-isyntax-rs/blob/3afb019138685404895a52461cc49d3c4de4d828/tests/test_pixel_engine.rs#L15) for all available open mode\n\nThe difference between the \"ficom\" and \"caching-ficom\" -> The latter creates a \".fic\" file with header information and so enable fast re-opening file but that implies a RW permission -> so the issue is not about mounted volumes but about permissions.\n\nHowever, I'm using the new SDK 2.0-L1 that runs under ubuntu 20.04 and not the SDK 2.0/ubuntu 18.04\n\nBest Regards",
                    "state": "closed",
